  "generated_text": "To find the intersection point of the two lines, we need to find the values of $t$ and $u$ that make the two parameterizations equal.\nSetting the two parameterizations equal, we have\n\\[\\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\\\ 1 \\end{pmatrix} + t \\begin{pmatrix} 2 \\\\ -3 \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} 5 \\\\ -9 \\end{pmatrix} + u \\begin{pmatrix} 4 \\\\ 2 \\end{pmatrix}.\\]\nThis gives us the system of equations\n\\begin{align*}\n1 + 2t &= 5 + 4u, \\\\\n1 - 3t &= -9 + 2u.\n\\end{align*}\nSolving this system, we find $t = 2$ and $u = 1$.\nTherefore, the intersection point is $\\boxed{\\begin{pmatrix} 5 \\\\ -5 \\end{pmatrix}}$.\nThe answer is: \\begin{pmatrix} 5 \\\\ -5 \\end{pmatrix}",
